From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GDmio <zhalin66@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:18:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/31] BlueOS: SystemUI: Power off and reboot screen

Instead of the stock spinner, an opaque screen in the theme colors with the
BlueOS logo: on power off its halo bobs and disappears (halos never fly away,
like in the game), then the logo and "See you, Sensei" fade out; on reboot
the halo spins ("Be right back, Sensei") until the boot animation lets it fall
back in. The system message and the reason for special reboots stay below.
The "powered-off finding" variant is unchanged. Logo drawables from
vendor/blueos/tools/make-logo-assets.py.

Change-Id: Ib5e0e573ed4b61caf79f6d8ed1bb3d060cf10850
